# =============================================================================
# 7. AI GENERATORS  —  the Teacher Hub, AI capture, the assistant
#
# `packages/ai` is the only place a model SDK is imported, for the same reason
# nothing outside packages/auth-provider imports Clerk: the vendor has to be
# changeable in one place.
#
# WITHOUT ANY OF THIS the Hub still works. `resolveGenerator()` falls back to
# the deterministic scaffold, which lays out a correctly timed lesson structure
# and honestly says it is not AI-written. That is the current default.
# =============================================================================

# WHICH generator runs. `template` (or unset) = the scaffold. `claude` = Anthropic.
#
# THIS is the switch, and it is separate from the keys ON PURPOSE.
# `resolveGenerator()` deliberately ignores ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: a key appearing in
# an environment is not the same as a curriculum knowledge base having been
# ingested and a prompt reviewed, and a generator that switches itself on when a
# variable appears is how an untested code path reaches a paying teacher.
#
# So you can safely set the keys below and leave this on `template` until the
# model path has actually been tried.
AI_GENERATOR=template

# Anthropic — generation. Lesson plans, quizzes, homework, and later the AI
# assistant. https://console.anthropic.com → API Keys
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# OpenAI — embeddings for the lesson-planner RAG pipeline
# (`text-embedding-3-small`), and a fallback generator if Anthropic is
# unavailable. https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
#
# Not needed for `AI_GENERATOR=claude`: the first curriculum store is relational
# rather than vector, because subject + grade + topic are EXACT lookups and
# similarity search is the wrong tool for a question with a known key. Embeddings
# earn their place once the corpus is prose — textbooks, past papers.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT A MODEL CALL COSTS YOU, AND WHAT STOPS IT RUNNING AWAY
#
# Every generation is metered against the AI credit ledger (migration 0132), and
# each ledger row records the model, the token counts and the real cost in USD.
# So a key in this file cannot quietly produce an unbounded bill: a school spends
# its tier's included allowance and then its purchased credits, and a standalone
# teacher spends their plan's. When the wallet is empty the call is refused with
# the shortfall stated, before the model is invoked.
#
# The prices and allowances are rows in `afritech.ai_credit_prices`,
# `ai_credit_packs` and `tier_ai_allowances` — changeable without a deployment,
# and none of them is hardcoded anywhere.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
